**How to implement.** In MuellerReconstruction (Domain) declare the CSV-load seam following the same [<ReferenceEquality>] proxy convention (ExperimentDataProxy.fs:43). Add the elevated row type MuellerRawRow = { experiment : string; captureIndex : int; capturedAt : System.DateTimeOffset; description : Angle; avgTotal : float }; the typed channel MuellerDataError = MalformedRow of reason : string | EmptyFile of reason : string; and [<ReferenceEquality>] type MuellerDataProxy = { tryLoadFamily : DataFilePath -> Result<MuellerRawRow list, MuellerDataError> }, reusing Experiments.DataFilePath (Experiments.fs:142). Supply an in-memory mock (canned rows keyed by DataFilePath.value) plus a mock-driven [<Fact>] in BerremanTests exercising the field, exactly like ExperimentDataProxyTests (ExperimentDataProxyTests.fs:38).

**Acceptance.** After the step, a mock-driven test MUST build a stub MuellerDataProxy, load canned rows through the exact tryLoadFamily signature, get a typed MuellerDataError for an unknown path (never a throw), and pass.
